ary-dues-are-cleared-report/articleshow/134899806.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134899806.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[SpiceJet is facing a serious operational crisis as approximately 40 pilots operating the Q400 aircraft have opted not to fly, protesting unpaid wages. The Airline Pilots' Association of India is backing their demand for fair treatment. Additionally, vendors are withholding necessary services because of delayed payments. The Directorate General of Civil Aviation is keeping a close eye on SpiceJet's mounting troubles as the airline navigates through its financial struggles.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/around-40-spicejet-q400-pilots-refuse-to-fly-until-salary-dues-are-cleared-report/articleshow/134899806.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/around-40-spicejet-q400-pilots-refuse-to-fly-until-salary-dues-are-cleared-report/articleshow/134899806.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T23:18:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134899959,imgsize-94390.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Uttarakhand CM Dhami meets Union minister Chouhan to seek approval for rural road expansion]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/uttarakhand-cm-dhami-meets-union-minister-chouhan-to-seek-approval-for-rural-road-expansion/articleshow/134899858.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134899858.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/uttarakhand-cm-dhami-meets-union-minister-chouhan-to-seek-approval-for-rural-road-expansion/articleshow/134899858.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/uttarakhand-cm-dhami-meets-union-minister-chouhan-to-seek-approval-for-rural-road-expansion/articleshow/134899858.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T23:14:57+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134899892,imgsize-81394.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[ICMR sets up high-altitude research centre in Keylong to study health risks in Himalayas]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/icmr-sets-up-high-altitude-research-centre-in-keylong-to-study-health-risks-in-himalayas/articleshow/134899765.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134899765.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Centre to study effects of low oxygen, extreme cold and climate change; research to cover soldiers, tribal communities, maternal and child health]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/icmr-sets-up-high-altitude-research-centre-in-keylong-to-study-health-risks-in-himalayas/articleshow/134899765.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/icmr-sets-up-high-altitude-research-centre-in-keylong-to-study-health-risks-in-himalayas/articleshow/134899765.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T23:14:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Anuja Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134899913,imgsize-201714.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Stay tuned for what comes next': US envoy says 'so much happening' in India-US ties]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/stay-tuned-for-what-comes-next-us-envoy-says-so-much-happening-in-india-us-ties/articleshow/134899651.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134899651.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The collaboration between India and the United States in sectors like defence, technology, and healthcare is on the rise. Conversations between Prime Minister Narendra Modi and US President Donald Trump indicate promising advancements. US ambassador to India, Sergio Gor, pointed out the critical military drills and financial investments enhancing the partnership. Additionally, the transfer of generic pharmaceuticals showcases India's trusted healthcare capacity, heralding promising economic prospects for both nations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/stay-tuned-for-what-comes-next-us-envoy-says-so-much-happening-in-india-us-ties/articleshow/134899651.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/stay-tuned-for-what-comes-next-us-envoy-says-so-much-happening-in-india-us-ties/articleshow/134899651.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T23:13:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134899697,imgsize-79914.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Uttarakhand CM unveils logo, anthem for Haridwar Kumbh-2027]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/uttarakhand-cm-unveils-logo-anthem-for-haridwar-kumbh-2027/articleshow/134899417.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134899417.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/uttarakhand-cm-unveils-logo-anthem-for-haridwar-kumbh-2027/articleshow/134899417.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/uttarakhand-cm-unveils-logo-anthem-for-haridwar-kumbh-2027/articleshow/134899417.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T22:47:39+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134899417,imgsize-213288.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Advance injustice': Allahabad HC flags POCSO Act's rigid application in minor couple cases]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/advance-injustice-allahabad-hc-flags-pocso-acts-rigid-application-in-minor-couple-cases/articleshow/134898819.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134898819.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Allahabad high court has urged the law commission to recommend amendments to the POCSO Act. This request aims to address cases involving minor couples while considering India's social realities. The court noted that strict law enforcement can promote injustice under certain circumstances. Moreover, the judges suggested allowing special judges flexibility to take individual cases into account.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/advance-injustice-allahabad-hc-flags-pocso-acts-rigid-application-in-minor-couple-cases/articleshow/134898819.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/advance-injustice-allahabad-hc-flags-pocso-acts-rigid-application-in-minor-couple-cases/articleshow/134898819.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T22:33:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134898984,imgsize-74391.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Cannot beat us, threaten us, frighten us': Rahul Gandhi thanks protesters after INDIA bloc march to SC]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cannot-beat-us-threaten-us-frighten-us-rahul-thanks-protesters-after-india-bloc-march-to-sc/articleshow/134898410.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134898410.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi thanked supporters for gathering in Delhi during the INDIA bloc march, aimed at raising awareness about electoral issues. The protest focused on alleged discrepancies and the Election Commission’s handling of voter deletions. Despite police barricades disrupting the march, Gandhi and fellow leaders moved forward by petitioning the Supreme Court for disclosure of Election Commission documents and measures to prevent unannounced voter deletions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cannot-beat-us-threaten-us-frighten-us-rahul-thanks-protesters-after-india-bloc-march-to-sc/articleshow/134898410.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cannot-beat-us-threaten-us-frighten-us-rahul-thanks-protesters-after-india-bloc-march-to-sc/articleshow/134898410.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T22:32:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134898959,imgsize-171464.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delhi's new protest venue Ramlila Maidan has just 3 dates available this year - check details]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhis-new-protest-venue-ramlila-maidan-has-just-3-dates-available-this-year-check-details/articleshow/134897459.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134897459.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhis-new-protest-venue-ramlila-maidan-has-just-3-dates-available-this-year-check-details/articleshow/134897459.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhis-new-protest-venue-ramlila-maidan-has-just-3-dates-available-this-year-check-details/articleshow/134897459.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T21:49:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134898150,imgsize-2087491.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[President Murmu appoints new governors for 6 states; 4 new, 2 moved]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/president-murmu-appoints-new-governors-for-6-states-4-new-2-moved/articleshow/134897545.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134897545.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/president-murmu-appoints-new-governors-for-6-states-4-new-2-moved/articleshow/134897545.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/president-murmu-appoints-new-governors-for-6-states-4-new-2-moved/articleshow/134897545.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T21:43:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134898075,imgsize-216596.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kerala govt to investigate alleged lapses in Rs 1.8 crore isolation ward project]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kerala-govt-to-investigate-alleged-lapses-in-rs-1-8-crore-isolation-ward-project/articleshow/134896877.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134896877.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Kerala's health minister has initiated an investigation into the discrepancies surrounding the construction of isolation wards. This project, previously approved by former health minister Veena George, has sparked criticism due to inefficiencies. Despite an allocation of Rs 250 crore for 88 wards, only 55 have been completed, with none ready for patient intake. The projects fall short on vital amenities, raising public safety concerns.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kerala-govt-to-investigate-alleged-lapses-in-rs-1-8-crore-isolation-ward-project/articleshow/134896877.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kerala-govt-to-investigate-alleged-lapses-in-rs-1-8-crore-isolation-ward-project/articleshow/134896877.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T21:06:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134896953,imgsize-42767.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Absolute faith in judiciary': Congress rejects Keralam party unit's post on CJI Surya Kant]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/absolute-faith-in-judiciary-congress-rejects-keralam-party-units-post-on-cji-surya-kant/articleshow/134896367.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/absolute-faith-in-judiciary-congress-rejects-keralam-party-units-post-on-cji-surya-kant/articleshow/134896367.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T20:33:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134896458,imgsize-70970.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cops detain anti-SIR protesters, assault journalists in Bengaluru]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cops-detain-anti-sir-protesters-assault-journalists-in-bengaluru/articleshow/134896362.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134896362.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cops-detain-anti-sir-protesters-assault-journalists-in-bengaluru/articleshow/134896362.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cops-detain-anti-sir-protesters-assault-journalists-in-bengaluru/articleshow/134896362.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T20:32:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chethan Kumar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134896453,imgsize-164368.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Four PoK residents killed in IED blast; security heightened in J&amp;K's Poonch]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/at-least-4-pok-residents-killed-after-powerful-explosion-jolts-line-of-control/articleshow/134896260.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134896260.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[At least four Pok individuals lost their lives in a blast caused by a suspected improvised explosive device. The incident occurred in the Satwal-Naki area of Hajira tehsil in Pakistan-occupied Kashmir. Initial reports indicate that the victims were cousins from Battal Mandhol village. Following the explosion, security forces heightened their vigilance across the Line of Control.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/at-least-4-pok-residents-killed-after-powerful-explosion-jolts-line-of-control/articleshow/134896260.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/at-least-4-pok-residents-killed-after-powerful-explosion-jolts-line-of-control/articleshow/134896260.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T20:27:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134896383,imgsize-148224.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ramlila Maidan: The ground where protests dealt blows to Congress government, twice]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ramlila-maidan-the-ground-where-protests-dealt-a-blow-to-congress-government-twice/articleshow/134895736.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134895736.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The other two designated venues are Burari Ground in north Delhi and CBD Ground in east Delhi. The move comes amid protests against the Election Commission over alleged irregularities in the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) of electoral rolls. While Jantar Mantar's removal marks a significant shift in the capital's protest landscape, Ramlila Maidan brings its own political history to the fore.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ramlila-maidan-the-ground-where-protests-dealt-a-blow-to-congress-government-twice/articleshow/134895736.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ramlila-maidan-the-ground-where-protests-dealt-a-blow-to-congress-government-twice/articleshow/134895736.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T20:16:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134896699,imgsize-284784.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Disclose EC files, set up audit panel': Rahul Gandhi, 10 INDIA bloc leaders move SC against CEC]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/disclose-ec-files-set-up-audit-panel-rahul-gandhi-10-india-bloc-leaders-move-sc-against-cec/articleshow/134895717.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134895717.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A march led by Rahul Gandhi and other opposition leaders reached the Supreme Court to contest electoral irregularities. The leaders filed a joint petition naming the Election Commission of India as a respondent. This petition challenges decisions related to the Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls. The opposition demands transparency and safeguards against voter deletions during the process.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/disclose-ec-files-set-up-audit-panel-rahul-gandhi-10-india-bloc-leaders-move-sc-against-cec/articleshow/134895717.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/disclose-ec-files-set-up-audit-panel-rahul-gandhi-10-india-bloc-leaders-move-sc-against-cec/articleshow/134895717.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T20:10:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pallavi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134895960,imgsize-209218.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Kerala, Karnataka, Telangana govts must resign’: Himanta's dare to Congress for contesting on ballot paper]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-kerala-karnataka-telangana-govts-must-resign-himantas-condition-for-contesting-on-ballot-paper/articleshow/134895689.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134895689.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-kerala-karnataka-telangana-govts-must-resign-himantas-condition-for-contesting-on-ballot-paper/articleshow/134895689.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-kerala-karnataka-telangana-govts-must-resign-himantas-condition-for-contesting-on-ballot-paper/articleshow/134895689.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-12T20:07:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134895937,